@zdch @SamWinterLevy really depends on whether there's any stable way to put the talent to use, but yes that's the most tricky part. in principle, London does show that it's possible - next to GDM, there's a lot of exciting non-frontier work happening that retains talent, and so talent-wise, the UK is in a great spot to consolidate and start sprinting. 

Paris might actually be almost the same. many countries won't have an analogous nexus, but then again, this doesn't necessarily need to be a country-level sprint. 

the question is really if you can find and encourage a sufficiently interesting activity for the meantime; fast-following might be one of them, etc.

