@thlarsen oh just to be clear I don't have a better plan, especially not under similar technical priors, and think this is a very admirable effort and a great piece! though I do feel like surely the bar for somewhat useful engagement must be lower than 'put in as much work as you guys and come up with something comparably sophisticated'. 

on 'best proposals given level of political will', though, I think that shifts my confusion to 'when do you postulate which level of political will for which kind of intervention', i.e. i feel like there are places where you postulate high political will for decisive intervention to specify paths (e.g. when we enter the plan A timeline), and places where you postulate low political will (redistribution differences by orders of magnitude). 

that's all very hard to model, so it's not necessarily a strike against the scenario - but it makes it hard to either evaluate this as 'the plan under near-optimal conditions' or as 'the plan under realistic political conditions'.
